.TH INVF-MIGRATE-V2 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf\-migrate\-v2 \- offline volume format v1 to v2 conversion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf\-migrate\-v2
.I image | device
.br
.B invf\-migrate\-v2
.B \-\-abort
.I image | device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf\-migrate\-v2
converts an InvariantFS volume from format v1 to v2 in place. The
conversion is crash\-safe: a house stage \(-> arm \(-> apply \(-> commit
protocol ensures that a crash at any point either rolls back to v1 or
completes the conversion on the next run.
.PP
The volume must be unmounted,
.BR CLEAN ,
not read\-only, with no live sweep checkpoint and no pending compaction.
.PP
The v2 format adds resolved pba fields to AST block entries, per\-file
heat counters, and the INO2 extension for full metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-abort
Roll back an armed\-but\-not\-yet\-applied conversion. Clears the CVT0
descriptor and returns the volume to its pre\-conversion v1 state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_DEV1
Path to the second device for two\-device (DEVT) volumes. Required when
converting a two\-device volume.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success or if already v2; 1 on error or refusal; 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf\-mkfs (8),
.BR invf\-sweep (8),
.BR invf\-rollback (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
